# llm-step's dependencies (format `<path> <name>`, path relative to this dir):
# the rustc worker factory that compiles it, the llm-client code crate it links,
# and THE TOOLS IT DRIVES — bash-tool, rgrep, bash (the tree-tool shell) and
# merge and run-and-update-ref. rustc DEPENDS on the runner pool itself and curries the built binary
# onto it, so no tool names a runner. LOCAL deps (mounted under DEEP-DEPS/ by
# deepening) rather than /std, so std has no ambient self-reference.
#
# The tools are declared HERE, rather than by whoever calls llm-step, because
# they are llm-step's dependencies: the caller should say what the turn is, not
# which shell the agent greps with. `.caos-expr` binds them, so resolving
# llm-step yields a step image with its tools already attached.
../rustc rustc
../llm-client llm-client
../bash-tool bash-tool
../rgrep rgrep
../bash bash
../merge merge
../run-and-update-ref run-and-update-ref
